{
  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::3754",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine appears to interact with multiple potassium channel subunits through a shared mechanism of binding to specific channels, leading to the activation of Delayed Rectifier Potassium Channel Activity. This activity is then associated with Kcnf1, suggesting a potential role for Guanidine in modulating Kcnf1 function. The consistent binding interactions across different target subunits (Kcna6, Kcnv2, Kcna7) imply that Guanidine may influence potassium channel activity through a common pathway, possibly by altering channel gating or conformation. The evidence suggests that Guanidine could act as a modulator of Kcnf1, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of potassium channels in cellular electrophysiology and suggests that Guanidine may have a broader impact on Kcnf1-dependent processes.",
